  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["V", "rrr", "s"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a78474cb-2df6-44bd-b86f-14191ad1c5fc"],
 " in Table 2 and Eqs. (20-22)  are represented by SphericalV\[Lambda]\
\[Lambda]\[Lambda], SphericalV\[Lambda]\[Lambda]\[Phi], SphericalV\[Lambda]\
\[Lambda]r, SphericalV\[Phi]\[Phi]\[Lambda], SphericalV\[Phi]\[Phi]\[Phi], \
SphericalV\[Phi]\[Phi]r, SphericalVrr\[Lambda], SphericalVrr\[Phi], and \
SphericalVrrr.\n3. The integral kernels are considered and the complete \
expressions should be presented as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"G\[Rho]", 
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", 
      SubscriptBox["\[Lambda]", "1"], 
      SubscriptBox["\[Lambda]", "2"]], 
     RowBox[{
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", 
       SubscriptBox["\[CurlyPhi]", "1"], 
       SubscriptBox["\[CurlyPhi]", "2"]], 
      RowBox[{
       SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", 
        SubscriptBox["u", "1"], 
        SubscriptBox["u", "2"]], 
       RowBox[{"\[Kappa]", " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", "Kernel", ")"}], 
        RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", 
         RowBox[{"u", "'"}]}], 
        RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", 
         RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "'"}]}], 
        RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", 
         RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", "'"}]}]}]}]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"36d44eac-199a-4a0e-acdc-fa1c7d776ace"],
 ". "
}], "Text",
